#### Step 1: Configure Error Detection

1. Integrate Lenses.io logs with central log aggregation system
   ```yaml
   # Logstash configuration for Lenses logs
   input {
     file {
       path => "/var/log/lenses/*.log"
       type => "lenses"
       codec => json
     }
   }
   filter {
     if [type] == "lenses" {
       grok {
         match => { "message" => "%{LOGLEVEL:severity} %{GREEDYDATA:error_message}" }
       }
     }
   }
   output {
     elasticsearch {
       hosts => ["elasticsearch:9200"]
       index => "lenses-logs-%{+YYYY.MM.dd}"
     }
   }
   ```
2. Define error patterns and signatures for top 20 most common errors
3. Configure pattern detection rules in log aggregation system
4. Set up threshold-based alerting for error rates
5. Test detection with historical data and adjust thresholds
6. Enable ML-based anomaly detection for new error patterns
